spec.section:
## U.8 Maintenance evidence and release gates

Each procedure emits a durable evidence bundle with:

* operation and dedupe identities, actor and authority;
* fence tuple and storage adapter capability result;
* exact source/target revisions, with nullable unknown values and reasons;
* config, artifact, archive and manifest digests;
* preflight, effect, failure-branch and post-effect reads;
* attempt/run identity, execution generation, terminal stop proof and capacity
  decision;
* scheduler registration state separately from read-only/immediate readiness;
* native archive adapter capability/version result without guessed values;
* retained gaps, tombstones, rollback lineage and operator decisions.

A maintenance report is **specified** evidence when it describes this contract,
**run** evidence only when these records were observed from a real target, and
**acceptance** evidence only when an authorized owner accepts the run. A generated
report or successful command cannot be promoted between classes. The release is
blocked while storage fencing/snapshot binding or native export/import capability
is unresolved, while any attempt/run lacks authoritative stop proof, or while
retention/backup evidence cannot be independently read back.


</div>
